<article class="env-corollary" id="05NZ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05NZ">Corollary <span data-tag="05NZ">3.2.4.15</span>.</a> Let $X$ be the colimit of a diagram of Kan complexes </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  X(0) \xrightarrow { f_0 } X(1) \xrightarrow { f_1 } X(2) \xrightarrow { f_2 } \cdots  \]
</div>
<p> If each of the morphisms $f_ n$ is nullhomotopic, then $X$ is contractible. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Theorem <a data-tag="04GJ" href="/tag/04GJ">3.2.4.3</a> (and Variant <a data-tag="050W" href="/tag/050W">3.2.4.12</a>), it will suffice to show that every morphism of simplicial sets $e: \operatorname{\partial \Delta }^ m \rightarrow X$ is nullhomotopic. Since $\operatorname{\partial \Delta }^ m$ is a finite simplicial set, the morphism $e$ factors through $X(n)$ for $n \gg 0$. The desired result now follows from our assumption that $f_ n: X(n) \rightarrow X(n+1)$ is nullhomotopic. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
